control_cli_events {"model": "gpt-6-luna", "events": "{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a16765-767b-7820-8c68-23d7f926137b\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"task_summary\\\":\\\"Extend the existing public API with `union_many(cases: list[tuple]) -> list`, preserving the day-1 API, adding unittest coverage, and recording verification evidence in HANDOFF.md.\\\",\\\"constraints\\\":[\\\"Process cases in order and return one result per call to `union`.\\\",\\\"Return [] when cases is empty.\\\",\\\"Propagate the first exception unchanged.\\\",\\\"Do not mutate cases or arguments.\\\",\\\"Keep the day-1 API compatible.\\\",\\\"Keep at least three passing unittest test methods in test_solution.py, including batch coverage.\\\",\\\"Update HANDOFF.md with the verification command and its observed result.\\\"],\\\"success_criteria\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-1\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"solution.py defines the typed union_many function.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def\\\\\\\\s+union_many\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\s*cases\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*list\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\[\\\\\\\\s*tuple\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\]\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*->\\\\\\\\s*list\\\\\\\\s*:\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-2\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation preserves the public union API and adds union_many without changing the day-1 API.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read the workspace files and assess whether solution.py adds the requested union_many(cases: list[tuple]) -> list while keeping the existing day-1 union API compatible. Judge only code and content visible in the files.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-3\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation processes cases in order, returns an empty list for no cases, propagates the first exception unchanged, and does not mutate cases or arguments.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read the workspace files and assess whether union_many calls union for each tuple's positional arguments in input order, returns [] for empty input, lets the first exception propagate unchanged, and avoids mutating cases or their arguments. Judge only code and content visible in the files.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"test_solution.py contains at least three unittest test methods, including coverage of union_many.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -c 'import ast; from pathlib import Path; tree = ast.parse(Path(\\\\\\\"test_solution.py\\\\\\\").read_text()); methods = [n for c in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(c, ast.ClassDef) for n in c.body if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef) and n.name.startswith(\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\")]; assert len(methods) >= 3; assert any(\\\\\\\"many\\\\\\\" in n.name.lower() or \\\\\\\"batch\\\\\\\" in n.name.lower() for n in methods)'\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"All unittest tests pass, including the required batch coverage.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-6\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"HANDOFF.md records the verification command and its observed result.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read HANDOFF.md and assess whether it records the unittest verification command and the observed result of running it. Do not infer execution from other files or terminal logs; assess only the recorded content.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-7\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"solution.py compiles successfully.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -c 'import ast; from pathlib import Path; tree = ast.parse(Path(\\\\\\\"test_solution.py\\\\\\\").read_text()); methods = [n for c in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(n, ast.ClassDef) for n in c.body if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef) and n.name.startswith(\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\")]; assert len(methods) >= 3; assert any(\\\\\\\"many\\\\\\\" in n.name.lower() or \\\\\\\"batch\\\\\\\" in n.name.lower() for n in methods)'\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Interpret the named paths solution.py, test_solution.py, and HANDOFF.md as relative paths within the runner-provided workspace.\\\",\\\"Those requested target files may not exist yet and may be created or updated.\\\",\\\"Assume `python -m unittest discover -v` is the appropriate discovery command, consistent with the supplied handoff context.\\\",\\\"The existing union API and its expected day-1 behavior are not specified in the request; preserve compatibility with the implementation present in the workspace.\\\",\\\"HANDOFF.md can record observed verification results after the checks have been run.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17724,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":971,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
